    "note": "**M1b.2 — fit-to-duration + Frame outline.** Two things from your last note:\n\n**1 · The walk now FITS the output length.** Before, 64 tiles needed ~67s of animation, so at `durationMs: 30000` the walk got cut off half-painted. Now the whole timeline is *uniformly compressed* to fill exactly whatever duration the output is — every tile paints, the camera follows all 64, nothing is truncated. Speed up/slow down by changing `durationMs` alone.\n\n**2 · Recommendation scales with tile count.** When you DON'T pin a duration, the template recommends one from how much must paint (~0.9s/step):\n\n| layout | steps | recommended |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2×2 | ~7 | ~7s |\n| 4×4 | ~21 | ~20s |\n| 8×8 | 73 | ~67s |\n\nSo this 8×8 *recommends* ~67s; you pinned **30s**, so it runs ~2.2× faster and still completes. (Omit `durationMs` to get the full-dwell recommendation.)\n\n**3 · Thin Frame outline** now rings the whole canvas — the bounds every tile paints into. It's part of the canvas content, so under zoom it scales + pans with the walk (you see the frame edge as you reach it). Tunable via the new `frameOutline` theme token; toggle with `showFrame`.",
